On a fresh clone, tess sync fails with not_initialized until the user runs tess init with the right prefix. When the database file is absent (not present and unreadable: that stays an error) and the remote has a sync ref, sync should create the database itself, taking the prefix from the remote's config file in the snapshot, then carry on with the normal fetch, merge, push. A copy with no remote ref and no database still needs tess init. Seen dogfooding on 2026-11-24: 19 issues synced only after a manual init.